  "conclusions": [
    "Actual archived parent/child joint frames reconstruct the same 7.3148mm open-chain retained-joint drift. It is not caused by using the omitted virtual closure edge, an incorrect body index, or nominal-anchor mismatch.",
    "add_link com=None is defined as body origin, shapes have density=0 and lock_inertia=True. No hidden COM translation enters pose-to-anchor conversion.",
    "FK analytic positions follow four-bar corners, positive Y rotation, side-center half-height and top-center full-height. Saved joint_q_start offsets and [theta,-theta,theta,-theta] are consistent with the directed hinges.",
    "Open and closed dynamics cover the same 0.5s with constant 0.02Nm active torque and gravity, no contacts. Angular velocities and the semi-implicit maximal-coordinate pose update make timestep refinement a justified diagnostic, but the cause is an inference until refinement is measured.",
    "Do not replace or label the original failed structural pair as passed. New timesteps need their own frozen protocol and run IDs; same duration/model/torque and original 0.5mm gate allow a convergence study without threshold relaxation."
  ],
